<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moldova</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Republic of Moldova</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moldova is a landlocked country in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chisinau">Chișinău</a>. Its core is the land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prut">Prut</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dniester">Dniester</a>, the eastern half of the medieval Principality of Moldavia, annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1812 as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a>. After union with Romania (1918–1940) and Soviet rule, it declared independence in 1991; the breakaway Transnistria region lies beyond its control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moldova.jpg" alt="Moldova" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gheorghe Vrabie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Moldova.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
